# TouchDesigner - Interactive Art Rules

## General Guidelines
- Write clean, maintainable networks and scripts
- Use clear operator and parameter names
- Comment complex expressions and Python
- Follow TouchDesigner best practices for real-time work
- Explain networks ELI5: in → change → out; define TOP/CHOP/SOP/DAT/COMP in one line when first used

## Network Style
- Keep operators focused and single-purpose
- Use consistent naming; avoid unnamed spaghetti
- Prefer reusable Components (`.tox`) over one giant `.toe`
- Optimize cooking / performance in interactive loops

## TouchDesigner Specifics
- Operator families: TOP (images), CHOP (signals), SOP (geometry), DAT (tables/text), COMP (containers)
- Know parameters vs. expressions vs. Python
- Wire interaction inputs (mouse, keyboard, MIDI, audio, sensors) clearly
- Use Perform Mode for showing work; Designer Mode for building
- Never overwrite a `.toe` / `.tox` without a dated backup first
- Prefer additive edits: build beside the old chain, then swap wires

## Project Structure
- One piece per subfolder when the work grows past a single sketch
- Prefer: main `.toe`, `tox/`, `assets/`, `notes/`, `exports/`
- Separate input / process / output sections in the network
- Keep media organized; don't commit crash dumps or huge unused files

## Learning & Testing
- Track milestones in `PROGRESS.md`
- Short notes: goal → what you built → what broke → what fixed it
- Test interactions and edge cases; note performance limits
- Document known bugs or limitations
